<a href="https://www.aqara.com/us/">Aqara</a> today introduced five new Matter-enabled smart lights compatible with Apple Home. The lights support Thread and Zigbee as well, and can be paired with Aqara sensors and switches.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/aqara-floor-lamp.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062180" /><br/>
The Floor Lamp T1 is a tall, rod-shaped light with a wall-wash effect. It has 18 controllable zones that can be set to different colors, and it supports 2000K to 9000K white light at up to 1,000 lumens.<br/>
<br/>
Aqara's LED Downlight T2 has a thin profile for low ceilings or retrofitting. It supports 16 million colors and 2000K to 9000K white light. The trimmable LED Strip T2 has 108 LEDs per meter and is ideal for use under cabinets and along shelves. Aqara says it delivers even light without visible hotspots. The light strip has 18 controllable zones every three meters for smooth color gradients.<br/>
<br/>
The Outdoor String Lights H1 are weatherproof for use on patios and decks. The lights have individually controllable zones with the same white light range as the other lights, and can adjust based on time of day, environment, and triggers from other smart home devices.<br/>
<br/>
Aqara also announced the Permanent Outdoor Lights H1 that can be used all year. The lights feature independently controlled LEDs and can be extended or cut to fit any roofline.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/aqara-permanent-lights.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1062181" /><br/>
